+# CONTRACT — Real-Time Collaborative Document Editor
+
+## A. Operational Transform core (`src/ot.ts`)
+- [ ] `applyOp(content, op)` applies an insert -> test: insert at pos splices text in
+- [ ] `applyOp` applies a delete -> test: delete removes `length` chars at pos
+- [ ] `applyOps` applies an ordered list (deletes desc-safe) -> test: multi-op list yields correct string
+- [ ] `validateOp` rejects malformed ops -> test: bad type/neg pos/oob/non-string text throws/returns error
+- [ ] `transformOp(a, against)` insert vs insert keeps both, deterministic shift -> test: concurrent inserts both survive, converge
+- [ ] insert vs delete shifts/clamps correctly -> test
+- [ ] delete vs insert (insert inside range) splits, preserves inserted text -> test
+- [ ] delete vs delete handles overlap (no negative length) -> test
+- [ ] `transformAgainstHistory(op, historyOps[])` folds op forward through versions -> test: concurrent ops converge to same string regardless
+
+## B. Persistence (`src/db.ts`)
+- [ ] schema initialized (documents, versions) -> test: tables exist
+- [ ] create/get/list/update/delete document -> test: CRUD round-trips
+- [ ] each content change records a version row -> test: versions increments
+- [ ] data survives reopening same db file -> test: write, close, reopen, read
+
+## C. REST API (`src/server.ts` via `createApp`)
+- [ ] `createApp(dbPath?)` returns `{app, start, stop, wss}` -> test: shape
+- [ ] `start(0)` returns a real port; `stop()` shuts cleanly -> test
+- [ ] POST /documents -> 201 with {id,title,content,version} -> test
+- [ ] POST with missing/invalid title -> 400 -> test
+- [ ] GET /documents -> 200 array -> test
+- [ ] GET /documents/:id -> 200 doc; unknown -> 404 -> test
+- [ ] PUT /documents/:id -> 200 updates title/content, new version -> test
+- [ ] DELETE /documents/:id -> 204; unknown -> 404 -> test
+- [ ] GET /documents/:id/versions -> 200 history array -> test
+
+## D. WebSocket realtime (`src/server.ts`)
+- [ ] connect to /documents/:id/ws -> receive `sync` {version, content} -> test
+- [ ] connect to unknown doc -> error message + close -> test
+- [ ] send op -> server applies, persists version, broadcasts `op` to all clients -> test
+- [ ] two clients editing concurrently converge to identical content (verified via REST) -> test
+- [ ] malformed op message -> `error` message, server does not crash -> test
+- [ ] 10 concurrent clients each inserting -> all chars preserved, converge -> test
+
+## E. Quality gates
+- [ ] `npm run build` compiles clean
+- [ ] `npm run lint` passes
+- [ ] `npm run test` all green
+- [ ] data survives full server restart (integration test)
